<script type="application/ld+json">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://sunconsultants.co.in/saso-saber-certification","headline":"What is SASO Certificate or SABER Certification","description":"Learn everything about SASO Certificate or SABER Certification in Saudi Arabia, including process, cost, documents, PCoC, SCoC, and requirements for exporters.","image":"https://sunconsultants.co.in/images/saso-saber-certification.jpg","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Sun Consultants & Engineers"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Sun Consultants & Engineers","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://sunconsultants.co.in/images/logo.png"}},"datePublished":"2026-04-30","dateModified":"2026-04-30","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://sunconsultants.co.in/saso-saber-certification"},"keywords":["SASO Certificate","SASO Certification Saudi Arabia","SABER Certificate Saudi Arabia","SALEEM Program","SASO registration","SABER process","SASO approval"]},{"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://sunconsultants.co.in/saso-saber-certification#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a SASO Certificate and why is it required?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization (SASO) Certificate is a mandatory document required for exporting regulated products to Saudi Arabia. It confirms that the product complies with Saudi safety, quality, and technical regulations. Without this certification, products cannot clear customs in Saudi Arabia. The certificate ensures consumer safety, environmental protection, and adherence to international standards. It also helps prevent counterfeit or substandard goods from entering the Saudi market, making it essential for legal and smooth trade operations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is SABER Certification in Saudi Arabia?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SABER Certification is an online conformity assessment system introduced under the SALEEM program. It is used to register products and obtain compliance certificates before exporting goods to Saudi Arabia. SABER is not a certification itself but a digital platform that facilitates issuing Product Certificate of Conformity (PCoC) and Shipment Certificate of Conformity (SCoC). It simplifies and digitizes the entire SASO certification process, ensuring faster approvals, transparency, and efficient customs clearance for imported products."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between SASO and SABER?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SASO refers to the regulatory authority that sets standards and technical regulations in Saudi Arabia, while SABER is the online system used to implement those regulations. In simple terms, SASO creates the rules, and SABER is the platform where businesses register products and obtain certification. Exporters must comply with SASO standards through the SABER system to get approval. Both are interconnected and essential for product compliance and legal entry into the Saudi Arabian market."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the SALEEM Program in Saudi Arabia?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SALEEM is the Saudi Product Safety Program designed to ensure that all products entering the Saudi market are safe and compliant. The word SALEEM means safe or risk-free. This program is managed by SASO and implemented through the SABER platform. It focuses on improving product quality, protecting consumers, and eliminating unsafe goods. Under SALEEM, every product must go through a structured certification process before it is allowed to be imported or sold in Saudi Arabia."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are PCoC and SCoC in SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PCoC (Product Certificate of Conformity) is issued for a specific product and confirms that it complies with Saudi standards. It is generally valid for one year. SCoC (Shipment Certificate of Conformity) is issued for each shipment and ensures that the goods being shipped match the approved product. Both certificates are mandatory under the SABER system. Without these certificates, shipments may be delayed, rejected, or denied entry at Saudi customs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who is responsible for SABER registration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Saudi importer is responsible for registering products on the SABER platform. They must have a valid Commercial Registration (CR) to initiate the process. However, exporters play a critical supporting role by providing technical documents, test reports, and product details. Without proper coordination between the importer and exporter, the certification process may face delays or rejection. Therefore, both parties must work together to ensure compliance with SASO regulations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What documents are required for SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To obtain SABER Certification, several documents are required, including a commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, product test reports, product images, and declaration of conformity. These documents help certification bodies evaluate whether the product meets Saudi standards. Accurate and complete documentation is crucial, as any errors or missing information can result in delays or rejection. Proper documentation also ensures smooth processing and faster approval through the SABER system."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does the SABER certification process take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The timeline for SABER certification depends on product type, documentation accuracy, and testing requirements. Generally, obtaining a Product Certificate (PCoC) can take a few days to a few weeks. Once the product is approved, generating a Shipment Certificate (SCoC) for each shipment is usually quicker and can be done within 1-3 days. Delays may occur if additional testing or corrections are required, so proper preparation is essential to speed up the process."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cost of SASO SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cost of SASO SABER Certification varies depending on product complexity, testing requirements, and certification body fees. Typically, the Product Certificate (PCoC) may cost between INR 50,000 to INR 2,00,000, while the Shipment Certificate (SCoC) ranges from INR 10,000 to INR 50,000 per shipment. Additional costs may include testing fees, documentation charges, and SABER platform fees. Businesses should plan their budget accordingly and work with experienced consultants to optimize costs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What products require SASO SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most regulated products exported to Saudi Arabia require SASO SABER Certification. These include electrical products, construction materials, automotive components, and consumer goods. Products are classified as regulated or non-regulated based on SASO technical regulations. Regulated products require certification, while non-regulated products may only need self-declaration. It is important to verify product classification before exporting to avoid compliance issues and shipment delays."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the benefits of SABER Certification for businesses?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SABER Certification offers multiple benefits for businesses, including easy access to the Saudi market, improved brand credibility, and compliance with international standards. It reduces shipment delays, ensures smooth customs clearance, and enhances customer trust. Companies with certified products gain a competitive advantage and can expand their market presence in Saudi Arabia. It also helps avoid penalties, product rejection, and legal issues during import processes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What challenges do companies face during SASO certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Companies often face challenges such as complex documentation, high certification costs, and evolving regulatory requirements. Technical compliance issues and delays in testing can also impact timelines. Additionally, lack of awareness about SABER procedures can lead to mistakes in product registration. To overcome these challenges, businesses should work with experienced consultants, maintain accurate documentation, and stay updated with the latest SASO regulations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can exporters directly apply for SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, exporters cannot directly apply for SABER Certification. The Saudi importer must register the product on the SABER platform. However, exporters are responsible for providing all required technical documents, test reports, and product specifications. Their role is crucial in ensuring compliance with SASO standards. Proper coordination between importer and exporter is essential for successful certification and timely shipment clearance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if a product does not have SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If a product does not have SABER Certification, it will not be allowed to enter Saudi Arabia. The shipment may be held at customs, rejected, or returned to the origin country. In some cases, penalties may also be imposed. Lack of certification can lead to financial losses, delays, and damage to business reputation. Therefore, obtaining proper certification before shipment is mandatory for smooth trade operations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can companies ensure successful SABER Certification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Companies can ensure successful SABER Certification by preparing accurate documentation, conducting pre-testing of products, and working with approved certification bodies. Staying updated with SASO regulations and using experienced consultants can significantly reduce errors and delays. Proper planning and coordination with the Saudi importer are also essential. Following best practices helps streamline the process, reduce costs, and ensure faster approvals."}}]}]}
